\import{fdip-macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}
\tag{fdip}
\taxon{Remark}
\title{Cylinders come from the residue rings}
\date{2026-11-07}

\p{The space #{X}, the ultrametric #{\delta}, and the
probability #{\eta} are constructed from the residue rings
and the uniform probabilities. The parameters #{\lambda} and
#{m} do not enter. The ball assignment #{M_k} is a separate
random functional. \ref{fdip-00C3} gives its finite additivity
on residue classes, and \ref{fdip-00C4} records that
countable additivity of that assignment on the Borel sets is
not proved.}
